WEBVTT

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:11.827
A definite integral adds up tiny pieces to find the signed area under a curve between

00:00:11.827 --> 00:00:13.042
two endpoints.

00:00:15.842 --> 00:00:23.695
First find an antiderivative, then evaluate it at the upper endpoint and subtract its

00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:26.282
value at the lower endpoint.

00:00:29.082 --> 00:00:35.202
For the integral of two x from zero to three, the area is nine.
